&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clara is the leading platform in Latin America for companies to execute and manage every payment operation.&lt;/strong&gt; More than 50,000 leading and fast-growing businesses run on our corporate cards, bill pay, financing and B2B payments, and in 2025 the Financial Times named Clara the region’s fastest-growing company. We’re passionate about helping every company we work with become more effective—and, through that, raising the region’s competitiveness. We’re ~400 people, backed by Notable Capital, Coatue, Kaszek, monashees, DST Global, ICONIQ, General Catalyst and Goldman Sachs, among others.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for an &lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;21&quot;&gt;AI Business Operations Expert&lt;/strong&gt; to join Clara Ops and architect a new era of how we run the company. This is a highly strategic, senior individual contributor role. You will be the visionary who spots where human effort can be optimized by machines—and then designs, deploys, and scales the enterprise-grade systems that make it happen. Sitting at the intersection of strategy, automation, and execution, you will work across leadership teams to eliminate friction, accelerate decisions, and raise the operational ceiling of Clara.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;You will report to the Global Head of Operations and act as a strategic partner to senior leaders in Product, Sales, Finance, and Engineering. You will own the full automation lifecycle: identifying the opportunity, architecting the solution, deploying it with advanced AI tooling, and measuring the enterprise-wide impact.&lt;/p&gt;
