&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI-powered prospecting &amp;amp; SDR tooling: design and ship agents/workflows that find, qualify, and engage prospects, and that get meetings on AEs&#39; calendars — using tools like Amplemarket, Clay, HubSpot, and LLM APIs, glued together with n8n or custom code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own lifecycle automation end to end: build and iterate on onboarding, activation, and retention flows across email, WhatsApp, and push, using Customer.io and our internal data stack, with AI doing the heavy lifting on personalization, timing, and content generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the SDR-to-AE handoff as a system, not a manual process: instrument lead scoring, routing, and handoff logic so reps spend time on conversations, not admin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype fast, validate faster: you&#39;re expected to go from idea to working internal tool in days, test it against real pipeline/activation metrics, kill what doesn&#39;t work, and scale what does.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally: work directly with Sales, SDR leadership, Lifecycle, and Data/Eng to identify where automation unlocks the most value, and to make sure what you build actually gets adopted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn data into iteration: use Metabase, HubSpot, and Customer.io data to measure what your builds are actually doing to CAC payback, meetings booked, activation rate, and pipeline generated — and report on it in plain, honest terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;+2 years of hands-on experience building automation, internal tools, or AI-powered products — not just using AI tools, but shipping things that use APIs, LLMs, or agent frameworks to do real work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with workflow/automation platforms (n8n, Zapier, Make, or equivalent) and comfort integrating APIs across systems (CRM, marketing automation, sales tooling).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working familiarity with CRM/lifecycle platforms such as HubSpot, Customer.io, or Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough technical fluency to read/write basic scripts (Python, JavaScript) or work closely with engineers to get something shipped — you don&#39;t need to be a software engineer, but you can&#39;t be blocked waiting for one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication in English; ability to explain what you built and why it matters to non-technical stakeholders and executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias toward building and testing over planning — you&#39;d rather ship a rough version this week than a perfect spec next month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in Lifecycle Marketing, RevOps, Sales Engineering, Product, or Software Engineering (any of these paths is fine — we care about what you&#39;ve built, not your job title history).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with sales engagement/AI prospecting tools (Amplemarket, Clay, Apollo, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic) and basic prompt engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in B2B SaaS or fintech, ideally with an SDR/AE motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup or small-team experience where you owned something end to end, from idea to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Portuguese proficiency (not required, but useful across our MX/BR/CO/AR footprint).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role: you&#39;ll split your time between the office, customers and home. We don&#39;t set a minimum number of office days for most roles — you&#39;ll spend time in the office naturally, and most days during your ramp-up or when your leader asks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Why Clara&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A high talent-density team&lt;/strong&gt; driven to make an impact in Latin America — low ego, high ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and stock options (ESOP) from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An annual learning budget and accelerated development paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;English is our working language, with Spanish and Portuguese every day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How we work&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clarity&lt;/strong&gt; — Open and direct communication: we say what we mean and give context where it matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simplicity&lt;/strong&gt; — If it can be simpler, it should be.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership&lt;/strong&gt; — We own everything we do, end to end. When something needs to happen, we don&#39;t wait.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pride&lt;/strong&gt; — We hold ourselves to a high standard, and it shows in what we deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABC (Always Be Changing)&lt;/strong&gt; — We adapt fast, embrace change, and keep learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusivity&lt;/strong&gt; — Diverse ideas, stories and perspectives build a better Clara.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the must-haves, apply — the nice-to-haves are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clara is the leading platform in Latin America for companies to execute and manage every payment operation.&lt;/strong&gt; More than 50,000 leading and fast-growing businesses run on our corporate cards, bill pay, financing and B2B payments, and in 2025 the Financial Times named Clara the region’s fastest-growing company. We’re passionate about helping every company we work with become more effective—and, through that, raising the region’s competitiveness. We’re ~400 people, backed by Notable Capital, Coatue, Kaszek, monashees, DST Global, ICONIQ, General Catalyst and Goldman Sachs, among others.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ready to start your career at full speed?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;What you’ll actually do&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship production code in your first weeks — real features, real customers, real money moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own features end to end: design, build, test, deploy, watch the metrics, fix what you broke.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI across your workflow — coding, debugging, testing, research, automating the boring parts — and push the frontier of how your team uses it, not just how you do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with Product, Design, and senior engineers. Ask the dumb question early; it’s cheaper than the wrong build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn the domain deeply. B2B fintech in LatAm is genuinely hard — multiple countries, multiple regulators, real consequences. That’s what makes it interesting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relocation to CDMX is encouraged and supported&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Two tracks — tell us which one fits you&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Engineering (fullstack, backend-leaning)&lt;/strong&gt; Backend services, APIs, and the interfaces on top of them. Our stack leans Java/Spring Boot, React, PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka, and AWS — but we don’t expect you to have used all of it. We expect you to have gone deep on &lt;em&gt;something&lt;/em&gt; and to pick up the rest fast.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; ML Engineering&lt;/strong&gt; Pipelines, models, and the systems that make them useful in production — risk scoring, fraud signals, spend intelligence. Python, SQL, and modern data tooling. Applied and in production, not just notebooks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Who you are&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re at the start of your software career.&lt;/strong&gt; Whether you finished your degree last month or took a different route to get here, this role is scoped for engineers without prior full-time software experience — and we’ll treat you accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A technical foundation.&lt;/strong&gt; CS, Software Engineering, Mathematics, Physics or similar — or equivalent ability you can demonstrate in code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ve built things, and you can point at them.&lt;/strong&gt; A GitHub, a deployed app, a repo people actually use, a hackathon win, a contribution to open source, a bot that solved a real problem for real users. One thing you built and can defend in depth beats a list of ten you touched.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re AI-native and you can prove it.&lt;/strong&gt; Not “I’ve used ChatGPT.” We mean: you’ve built &lt;em&gt;with&lt;/em&gt; AI — agents, RAG, evals, fine-tunes, a tool that automates something you were sick of doing — and you use AI tools every day in how you code. Come ready to show us the artifact and walk us through the decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong fundamentals.&lt;/strong&gt; Data structures, algorithms, systems thinking. Competitive programming (ICPC, OMI, Codeforces), a strong thesis, or serious research all count and we want to hear about them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;English proficiency.&lt;/strong&gt; English is our corporate language — you’ll read, write, and discuss technical work in it daily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; You surface problems before they become blockers, you push things over the finish line, and you don’t wait to be told what to do. This is the single trait we screen hardest for.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
