&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clara is the leading platform in Latin America for companies to execute and manage every payment operation.&lt;/strong&gt; More than 50,000 leading and fast-growing businesses run on our corporate cards, bill pay, financing and B2B payments, and in 2025 the Financial Times named Clara the region’s fastest-growing company. We’re passionate about helping every company we work with become more effective—and, through that, raising the region’s competitiveness. We’re ~400 people, backed by Notable Capital, Coatue, Kaszek, monashees, DST Global, ICONIQ, General Catalyst and Goldman Sachs, among others.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Credit Analysis Lead&lt;/strong&gt; to own the credit analysis function for our B2B clients in Brazil. You’ll lead a team of credit analysts who assess companies and recommend credit lines, and you’ll be accountable for the &lt;strong&gt;quality, speed, and consistency of every credit decision&lt;/strong&gt; that comes through the desk.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your ownership starts when a credit request enters the credit desk (new client, limit increase, renewal, or triggered review) and covers everything until a &lt;strong&gt;credit decision is issued&lt;/strong&gt; (approve / decline / amount and terms) and later &lt;strong&gt;maintained&lt;/strong&gt; (renewals, limit adjustments, periodic reviews). Other teams own the steps before and after that path — but you still own making sure the whole flow works: if something upstream delays a case or something downstream breaks the experience, it’s your problem to raise and get fixed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll partner closely with Sales, Risk, Product/Data and Collections to keep the credit flow fast, the portfolio healthy and the analysis workflow scalable&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the credit analysis team&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach and develop a team of credit analysts: hiring, onboarding, training, calibration and capacity/SLA planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own daily desk operations: intake and triage of requests, prioritization by segment and exposure, queue management and turnaround-time SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the credit approval cadence and act as escalation point for borderline, complex or high-exposure cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perform and quality-review B2B credit analysis&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze Brazilian companies’ financial health: financial statements and cash flow (DRE, balanço, DFC), revenue and margin trends, leverage, liquidity, working capital cycle and seasonality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read the whole economic group: parent and related entities, sócios and partners, cross-exposure and consolidated exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret Brazilian credit bureau and public data, understanding the limits and false positives of each source.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Issue or recommend credit limits and terms within a delegated authority (alçada), documenting the rationale clearly; escalate above authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle review triggers: renewals, limit increases/decreases, negative news, and deterioration in related accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the voice of the front line for credit strategy&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the closest point to real client cases: surface patterns, edge cases and segment realities back to the teams that own credit policy, scorecards and portfolio strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give structured, data-backed feedback on where policy, rules or score cutoffs don’t match what the analysis actually shows — and propose concrete adjustments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and improve the metrics that matter for your team: approval rate, TAT, override rate and decline-reason distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flag early signs of deterioration in the cases your team touches, so the owners of portfolio monitoring can act on them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive automation and simplification&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Data and Engineering to automate bureau pulls, decision rules and scorecards, and to simplify the analyst workflow so the team scales without adding headcount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously re-draw the line between what gets auto-approved and what an analyst must review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build your own analyses and lightweight tools (AI-assisted coding, scripts, no-code/low-code) to take manual work out of your team’s day-to-day — you don’t need to be an engineer, but you should be able to ship something yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;“We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.”&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Must haves:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in credit risk / corporate credit analysis in Brazil, with hands-on financial-statement and cash-flow analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years leading or coordinating a credit analysis team (manager, coordinator or supervisor), with a track record of developing analysts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of Brazilian credit bureau data and scoring, including what each source does and doesn’t tell you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within credit policy and approval alçadas, with a strong instinct for when a case deserves to be challenged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with data: advanced spreadsheets plus, ideally, SQL and a BI tool (Looker, Metabase, Tableau) to pull and validate your own numbers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and hands-on with tooling: able to build your own small automations, scripts or internal tools (AI-assisted coding, no-code/low-code) to remove manual work from your team. We’re not hiring an engineer, but we do expect you to ship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication and attention to detail; able to defend decisions to commercial and risk stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fintech or B2B credit scale-up experience in LATAM; lending to PMEs and mid-market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to scorecard/model development, monitoring and credit model governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Google Workspace, Zendesk and HubSpot (or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spanish (or willingness to learn).&lt;/li&gt;
