&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, implementing, or optimizing fraud detection strategies and automated decisioning frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of machine learning, AI-driven fraud detection, and automation, with the ability to collaborate effectively with technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with fraud detection platforms, rule engines, case management systems, or risk decisioning tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, with experience using &lt;strong&gt;SQL&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Python&lt;/strong&gt;, or similar tools to analyze fraud patterns, evaluate detection performance, and identify opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining and monitoring fraud detection KPIs, including detection rates, false positives, automation coverage, and model effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of model governance, explainability, risk controls, and human oversight in automated decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven role-specific execution with an ability to influence cross-functional and regional stakeholders without direct management authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptability to fast-changing environments, strong ownership, problem-solving skills, and the ability to translate complex fraud challenges into practical, scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience or strong interest in using AI tools to automate workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
