&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clara is the leading platform in Latin America for companies to execute and manage every payment operation.&lt;/strong&gt; More than 50,000 leading and fast-growing businesses run on our corporate cards, bill pay, financing and B2B payments, and in 2025 the Financial Times named Clara the region’s fastest-growing company. We’re passionate about helping every company we work with become more effective—and, through that, raising the region’s competitiveness. We’re ~400 people, backed by Notable Capital, Coatue, Kaszek, monashees, DST Global, ICONIQ, General Catalyst and Goldman Sachs, among others.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT CLARA&lt;/strong&gt; Clara is the leading spend management platform for businesses in Latin America. We provide corporate cards, expense management, and AP automation across Mexico, Colombia, and Brazil. Our mission: give every company in Latin America complete control of their spending.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Small, high-powered squads. Senior engineers. AI tools baked into how we work. The person running product for a squad doesn&#39;t just write specs — they own outcomes end to end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt; SPEI is Mexico&#39;s primary interbank payment rail. For Clara customers, it powers everything from supplier payments to tax disbursements to payroll runs. BillPay Mexico is the product that makes this seamless — domestic and cross-border transfers, payment tracking, reconciliation, and the compliance layer that keeps everything clean with SAT, CNBV, and banking partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a squad lead role reporting directly to the Global Product Director. You&#39;ll own the full BillPay product experience for the Mexican market: payment flows, bank partner integrations, disbursement reliability, and the back-office tooling that supports operations and finance. You&#39;ll work closely with engineers, design, banking infrastructure, compliance, and enterprise sales teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires physical presence in Mexico City — we&#39;re in active conversations with banking partners and regulators, and showing up in person matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own discovery, prioritization, and outcomes for the BillPay MX squad — understand why payment success rates move, why reconciliation breaks, and why customers churn, not just what launched&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build deep understanding of SPEI infrastructure: clearing windows, return codes, CLABE validation, and failure propagation — and extend that to cross-border flows (FX rails, correspondent banking, settlement timing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and evolve banking partner relationships from a product perspective: know what integration contracts allow, where bottlenecks are, and what needs to be negotiated next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own compliance signals: SAT requirements, CNBV guidelines, and PLD/AML obligations for transfer products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track the metrics that matter: payment success rate, settlement time, reconciliation error rate, time-to-resolve for failed transfers, and BillPay contribution to customer retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and iterate on disbursement workflows — from single transfers to bulk payment runs for hundreds of suppliers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype with AI tools (Cursor, Claude Code, v0) before committing engineering time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute straightforward code changes (copy, config, feature flags, simple UI, analytics) through engineer-reviewed PRs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in Git daily: read PRs, understand what shipped, follow what&#39;s blocked&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE&#39;RE LOOKING FOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Experience&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in product management, with at least 2 years owning a payments, banking, or financial infrastructure product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of shipping products that moved business metrics — not just features that launched&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with payment rails, banking APIs, or financial infrastructure at a product level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with engineers as peers, not through project managers or coordinators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Domain knowledge — payments&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of SPEI: clearing cycles, error handling, CLABE structure, and how to design reliable retry and fallback flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cross-border payment rails: FX conversion, correspondent banking, SWIFT or alternative rails, and associated compliance overhead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Mexican banking regulations: SAT CFDIs, CNBV licensing implications, AML/PLD obligations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating with or managing bank correspondent relationships from a product side&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands how reconciliation works end to end: what breaks it, how to design around it, and how to give finance teams the visibility they need&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Technical fluency&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can prototype a working concept using AI coding tools (Cursor, Claude Code, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with Git: branches, commits, PRs, reading diffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can read code well enough to follow what a PR does and ask informed questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands API integrations, webhooks, async payment flows, and idempotency patterns at a conceptual level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Product fundamentals&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong discovery instincts — finds the real problem before designing a solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-literate: comfortable with SQL, funnel analysis, and experiment design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communicator in both Spanish and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management across engineering, banking partners, compliance, finance, and enterprise sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Mindset&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency — defaults to action over process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treats AI tools as core workflow, not a novelty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in ambiguous regulatory environments — knows how to make progress without waiting for perfect clarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE TO HAVE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP integrations (SAP, Oracle, Aspel, CONTPAQi) from a payments or AP perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Banxico&#39;s regulatory framework and SPEI operating rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-currency or cross-border payment products at production scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL fluency beyond &quot;can write a query&quot; — you&#39;ve built your own dashboards and done your own reconciliation analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LANGUAGES&lt;/strong&gt; Full bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish required. Native or near-native Spanish is a hard requirement — not a nice-to-have. You&#39;ll work in English with cross-functional teams across LatAm and in Spanish with banking partners, regulators, and customers in Mexico. Portuguese is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
