&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clara is the leading platform in Latin America for companies to execute and manage every payment operation.&lt;/strong&gt; More than 50,000 leading and fast-growing businesses run on our corporate cards, bill pay, financing and B2B payments, and in 2025 the Financial Times named Clara the region’s fastest-growing company. We’re passionate about helping every company we work with become more effective—and, through that, raising the region’s competitiveness. We’re ~400 people, backed by Notable Capital, Coatue, Kaszek, monashees, DST Global, ICONIQ, General Catalyst and Goldman Sachs, among others.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Fullstack/Backend Engineer focused on QA Automation&lt;/strong&gt; — a software engineer who builds the infrastructure, frameworks, APIs, and tooling that make automated quality possible at Clara. This is an &lt;strong&gt;engineering craft&lt;/strong&gt; role (closer to SDET / SET / platform engineer than classic manual QA): you write production-grade code that enables pods and QA to generate, run, and trust automated tests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You build and maintain the systems behind Clara&#39;s QA platform: Playwright-based frameworks, services and APIs that support test execution and reporting, CI wiring, and internal tools (e.g. test case / run persistence on Clara&#39;s React/Next stack). You collaborate with the QA Automation Lead, Pod Leads, and product engineers so automation is reusable, agent-ready, and owned as real software — not a pile of brittle scripts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Own&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt; — Design and implement shared frameworks and libraries for web/API automation (Playwright preferred), with stable selectors, modular architecture, and clear extension points for pods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tooling &amp;amp; services&lt;/strong&gt; — Build backend APIs and fullstack components that store test cases, record run results, expose reports, and integrate with delivery workflows (e.g. Linear webhooks, Slack notifications, GitHub Actions).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enablement for AI-assisted QA&lt;/strong&gt; — Structure frameworks and contracts so agents and CLIs can generate and execute specs reliably (ticket → matrix → runnable tests → evidence).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CI/CD for quality&lt;/strong&gt; — Implement and harden pipelines for smoke and regression suites; reduce flakiness; make failures diagnosable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering quality of test code&lt;/strong&gt; — Treat automation as a first-class codebase: reviews, tests for helpers, versioning, documentation, and refactoring for maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnership&lt;/strong&gt; — Work with QA engineers on adoption and with product engineers on testability (APIs, &lt;code&gt;data-testid&lt;/code&gt; / ARIA, environments, test data hooks).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Distinguishes This Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stronger software engineering depth than a traditional QA Engineer JD (services, APIs, data models, frontend for internal tools).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focused on &lt;strong&gt;enabling&lt;/strong&gt; automation at scale — not owning all manual exploratory testing for every pod.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Technical Skills&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of software development experience (backend and/or fullstack), with demonstrable automation or developer-tooling delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;TypeScript/JavaScript&lt;/strong&gt; for Playwright (or equivalent E2E frameworks) and willingness to work in Clara&#39;s backend stack (&lt;strong&gt;Java / Spring Boot&lt;/strong&gt;) where services or integrations require it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and maintaining &lt;strong&gt;test automation frameworks&lt;/strong&gt; (web and API); understanding of the test pyramid and when to prefer API vs UI coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backend fundamentals: REST APIs, relational databases, authentication basics, and clean service boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fullstack comfort for internal tools: React / Next.js (or similar) for dashboards and test-management UIs is a strong fit with Clara&#39;s internal scaffold direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD experience (GitHub Actions or similar), Docker familiarity, and Git-based collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to debug flaky tests, environment issues, and integration failures systematically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Soft Skills&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builder mindset: you ship frameworks and tools that other engineers adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear documentation and communication with QA and product engineering partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity and iterating from working prototypes to reliable platform pieces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative code review habits; you raise the bar on test-code quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good English (written and verbal); Spanish is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior SDET / SET / Test Infrastructure Engineer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobile automation (Appium) or BrowserStack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow orchestration (n8n), Linear/GitHub API integrations, or AI/agent tooling for test generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS and observability basics for running automation reliably in shared environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fintech / payments domain exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience replacing external test-management tools with internal systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a remote-first role: you&#39;ll work from home day to day. You&#39;ll ramp up in person with the team, and come together in person for team moments, events and customer visits through the year.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Why Clara&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A high talent-density team&lt;/strong&gt; driven to make an impact in Latin America — low ego, high ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and stock options (ESOP) from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An annual learning budget and accelerated development paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;English is our working language, with Spanish and Portuguese every day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How we work&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clarity&lt;/strong&gt; — Open and direct communication: we say what we mean and give context where it matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simplicity&lt;/strong&gt; — If it can be simpler, it should be.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership&lt;/strong&gt; — We own everything we do, end to end. When something needs to happen, we don&#39;t wait.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pride&lt;/strong&gt; — We hold ourselves to a high standard, and it shows in what we deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABC (Always Be Changing)&lt;/strong&gt; — We adapt fast, embrace change, and keep learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusivity&lt;/strong&gt; — Diverse ideas, stories and perspectives build a better Clara.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the must-haves, apply — the nice-to-haves are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clara is the leading platform in Latin America for companies to execute and manage every payment operation.&lt;/strong&gt; More than 50,000 leading and fast-growing businesses run on our corporate cards, bill pay, financing and B2B payments, and in 2025 the Financial Times named Clara the region’s fastest-growing company. We’re passionate about helping every company we work with become more effective—and, through that, raising the region’s competitiveness. We’re ~400 people, backed by Notable Capital, Coatue, Kaszek, monashees, DST Global, ICONIQ, General Catalyst and Goldman Sachs, among others.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Solutions Engineer to be the technical owner of our enterprise sales motion and our most strategic accounts. You&#39;ll partner with Account Executives to win complex deals, lead the design and delivery of enterprise integrations, and stay close to key accounts after go-live — making sure Clara&#39;s platform runs well and continues to grow inside their organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-lifecycle role — and it&#39;s for someone who builds. You&#39;ll run technical discovery and POCs in the sales phase, own integration delivery from scoping to handoff, and act as the primary technical point of contact for a portfolio of enterprise accounts. &lt;strong&gt;But beyond execution, we expect you to constantly challenge how we work: shipping internal tools, automating what slows the team down, and using AI as a genuine force multiplier to reach an order of magnitude more impact with every integration we deliver.&lt;/strong&gt; The common thread across everything is ownership: you don&#39;t wait to be told, and you don&#39;t throw things over a fence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Win deals alongside the sales team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Partner with Account Executives in enterprise sales cycles — running technical discovery, demos, and proof-of-concept engagements that remove blockers and accelerate close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Translate Clara&#39;s platform capabilities into concrete technical answers for both IT architects and business stakeholders (CFOs, finance leads, procurement teams).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Scope integrations early in the sales cycle — mapping customer systems, data flows, and technical requirements to a realistic implementation plan before contracts are signed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Support RFP/RFI responses and security questionnaires for enterprise prospects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design and deliver integrations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Own the end-to-end design and delivery of complex integrations between Clara&#39;s platform and enterprise ERP systems (SAP, Oracle, TOTVS, Omie, Sankhya).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Build and configure integration connectors, data mappings, and workflows using Clara&#39;s APIs and integration framework.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Coordinate with customer technical teams, Clara&#39;s Product and Engineering squads, and third-party implementation partners throughout delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Drive clean go-lives — delivering runbooks, monitoring configuration, and support playbooks before marking an integration as done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Identify patterns across customer integrations and feed them back into the platform through Product and Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build for the team and for clients&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Proactively identify friction in how the SE team operates — then build tools, automations, and workflows to eliminate it, not work around it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Ship internal tooling that gives the team real leverage: automated scoping flows, demo environments, integration health dashboards, AI-assisted documentation, or anything else that moves the needle on team productivity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Develop reusable assets from what you learn in the field — integration blueprints, connector templates, scoping playbooks, and demo environments — so that field knowledge compounds into shared team capability; every complex engagement should leave behind something the team can build on next time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Use AI coding tools (Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, and equivalents) as a daily part of your workflow — to scaffold integrations faster, automate repetitive mapping work, generate boilerplate, and prototype solutions that would otherwise take days.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Raise the bar on how clients experience our integration capability: what we demo, how we document, and how we make Clara&#39;s technical sophistication visible should constantly improve because of what you build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Challenge the status quo — if there&#39;s a faster, smarter way to deliver an integration or run a POC, find it, build it, and share it with the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the technical relationship for strategic accounts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Act as the primary technical point of contact for a portfolio of enterprise accounts after go-live — proactively managing integration health, surfacing risks before they escalate, and connecting customers to the right internal teams when needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Identify opportunities for optimization and expansion within existing accounts and bring them to the commercial team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Maintain strong relationships with technical and business stakeholders at key accounts, ensuring their satisfaction and enabling renewal and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- 5+ years in a technical customer-facing role — Solutions Engineer, Pre-Sales Engineer, Technical Account Manager, or equivalent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Active daily use of AI coding tools — Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, or equivalent — to accelerate development and automate repetitive work; you treat AI as a force multiplier, not a novelty.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Demonstrated experience running technical sales cycles: you&#39;ve helped close enterprise deals, not just supported them from the sidelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Hands-on experience designing and delivering ERP integrations (SAP, Oracle, TOTVS, or similar) — including API design, data mapping, and error handling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Deep fluency in integration patterns: REST APIs, webhooks, OAuth, event-driven architectures&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong communication in Portuguese and English — you can calibrate between technical depth and business impact depending on who&#39;s in the room.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Track record of owning technical relationships with enterprise customers over time, not just during implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Demonstrated builder instinct: you&#39;ve shipped internal tools, scripts, or automations that improved how a team worked, not just delivered what was scoped.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience in fintech, payments, or financial data infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Familiarity with integration platforms (n8n, Dell Boomi, or similar).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Exposure to cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Spanish proficiency is a strong plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience managing third-party vendors or ERP implementation partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Familiarity with virtual card network (VCN) programs — including card issuance APIs, spend controls (velocity limits, merchant restrictions, geography rules), and transaction reconciliation flows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
